            <title>[LU-21014] FLR-EC: Fix overstriping bug in EC allocations</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21014</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;With overstriping, lod_check_and_reserve_ost() lets the RR loop reuse&lt;br/&gt;
an OST while lag_ost_avail says unique OSTs remain. That count includes&lt;br/&gt;
OSTs RR skips, such as inactive or degraded ones, so an EC data&lt;br/&gt;
component can reuse an OST before lod_ec_add_data() takes over, which&lt;br/&gt;
repeats the placed stripes assuming they are unique and so puts two&lt;br/&gt;
stripes of a raid set on one OST, e.g. -C 13 --ec 5+2 on 8 OSTs with&lt;br/&gt;
one down.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Leave all OST reuse for EC components to lod_ec_add_data() and&lt;br/&gt;
lod_ec_add_parities(), which keep each raid set on distinct OSTs.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
